    "text_delta": "rtlist, I am keen to understand the panel’s evaluation against the competency framework to support my ongoing professional development.\"*\n\n2. **Request objective scoring and notes:**\n   Depending on your jurisdiction’s civil service guidelines (or data protection/subject access rules), you are typically entitled to your competency scores and the panel’s summary notes. Focus your review entirely on:\n   * How you scored against each advertised competency.\n   * Specific areas where the panel noted gaps or where other candidates demonstrated stronger evidence.\n\n3. **Assess the feedback objectively:**\n   * If the feedback outlines clear, competency-based reasons why another candidate scored higher, treat it as constructive guidance for your next senior-level application.\n   * If there is clear evidence of a **procedural irregularity** (e.g., standard civil service recruitment code rules were violated, scoring criteria were altered mid-process, or non-merit factors were cited), then you can explore your civil service's formal appeal or ombudsman process. Any such claim, however, must rest on documented procedural faults or discriminatory acts, not the demographic makeup of the panel.\n",
